= Hexagon source intake — Crypto Autoresearcher
2026-10-30 · source curation and native integration pointers

The complete dated cs.CC snapshot contains 22 works. Their primary PDFs were
retrieved and hashed, and source statements and relevant limits were reviewed.
Twenty-two versioned literature notes retain those reported claims and their
assumptions. A separate direct review of Petit–Kosters–Messeng, PKC 2016,
sections 3.1–3.4, supersedes the earlier abstract-only PKM note KN-LIT-025.
Knowledge-map.json identifies every new note; the source indexes are regenerated.

#image("integration.svg", width: 100%)

*Executable pointers.* The paired crypto change provides exact divisor-prefix
factoring with the existing OpenAI-based counter, exhaustive weighted cost
profiles, three structured prime-field factor-base recipes, a native searchable
catalog and two finite counterexample controls. Cryptanalysis imports the new
tensor modules. These are bounded software integrations; the source papers'
asymptotic claims are not inherited by these implementations.

*Validation.* Sixteen source-index unit tests and both generated-index checks
pass. The full ledger validator refuses the sparse checkout; its bypass was
not used and full-corpus validation remains unpassed locally. The checked-in
logs retain those exact outcomes. No hypothesis, finding, goal, disposition,
frontier or attack-cost status is promoted, and there is no new performance data.

*Open work.* Complete proof audits and Lean builds, the general tensor
correctness/complexity audit, the Anthropic engine port, subexponential weighted
contraction and the fast Subset Sum/3SUM engines remain unperformed. The paired
crypto report at research/hexagon_cscc_20261030/ contains all 22 source entries,
their implementation status and the development verification record.
